From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: include the SAE header for plain DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT builds

SEC_CONFIG carries struct pwd_id_list and struct sae_capability whenever
DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT is set, but sec_cmm.h only included sae_cmm.h for
SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT, which is restricted to APCLI_SUPPLICANT builds. Compiling
the AP driver with WPA3 enabled and APCLI supplicant disabled therefore
failed with "field 'pwd_id_list_head' has incomplete type". Include the
header for both cases, matching the guards used by the members themselves.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/common/security/sec_cmm.h
@@ -12,7 +12,13 @@
 
 #include "security/owe_cmm.h"
 
-#ifdef SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT
+/*
+ * struct pwd_id_list / struct sae_capability are members of SEC_CONFIG when
+ * DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT is set, so the header has to be pulled in for that case
+ * too.  SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT is only defined for APCLI_SUPPLICANT builds, which
+ * left the plain cfg80211 AP build with incomplete types.
+ */
+#if defined(SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT) || defined(DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT)
 #include "security/sae_cmm.h"
 #endif
 
